 "test_read": "no test frame is assembled or evaluated, no test score or metric is read. What each command reads. check-machine: this configuration and, through pad_anet_comparison.load_config, the configuration of PR A with the files it pins (no frame, no checkpoint); the trial record of PR A. check-inputs and run: this configuration; the configuration of PR A and what pad_anet_comparison.load_config and load_inputs read (the C2 pre-registration and the configurations it pins, the PR #27 configuration, the C2 trial record, the public status.json and results.json of the C2 evaluation, the architecture file, the code); the code files pinned here and this file; the status.json and trial.json of the official C5 trial and the SHA256SUMS of the PR A package that lists them; run_matrix.csv, run_order.csv and run_caps.csv, compared with the files regenerated from the configuration of PR A, the public files of the C2 evaluation and the trial; the PR #28 configuration (bytes, for its SHA-256); what pad_arch_comparison.load_inputs reads (its TEST_READ: the five M2 manifests, the cache hashed whole, the extracted frames file loaded whole, both frame files also holding frames of the held-out subjects, the cells and folds runs, the two accepted LivenessNet runs); the 12 training cards of arm B of each accepted run (keys of the fitting and dev frames); with --estimator-check, the status.json and estimator_check.json of a check-estimator record. run, in addition: the image arrays of the cache, loaded whole into the frame store; of all the frames it assembles only the fitting and dev frames of arm B (an explicit check refuses any other role); it reads back its own checkpoints. check-estimator: what pad_arch_run.cmd_check_estimator reads (the configurations of PRs #27 and #28, what nuaa_bn_recalibration.load_inputs and nuaa_bn_test.load_bnrecal read: the M2 manifests, cache and extracted frames file, the cells and folds runs, the parent run at patience 4 with per model card, dev scores, threshold and checkpoint, its aggregate.json only as bytes, the BNRECAL run with dev and fitting rows only); it assembles only fitting and dev frames. No command loads the fold schema (fold<k>_test.csv) or opens a <model>_test_scores.csv"
